    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0156" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d92-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-03">3 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Former Naval Person to President
                        Roosevelt personal and most secret
                    Number 488. Your number 406.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d92-f2"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>I and the British Staffs will await you in Cairo on 22nd.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>We think it necessary that the British and United States Staffs should
                        consult together before any triple conference with the Russians take[s]
                        place, and that when it takes place there should be a responsible Russian
                        delegation and not a mere observer. I should be grateful if you would let me
                        know whether you agree with this.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d92-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d92-f1-content">
